  "id": "Compound::DB06292 - Gene::6523",
  "verbalization": "Dapagliflozin, a sodium-glucose cotransporter (SGLT) inhibitor, is shown to bind to Slc5a2 and Slc5a4, which are both involved in glucose and sodium transport. These transporters are part of the Slc5a family, and their participation in glucose-sodium symport activity and Na+-dependent glucose transport is linked to Slc5a1. The evidence suggests that Dapagliflozin may influence Slc5a1 through its interaction with these related transporters, potentially modulating glucose uptake and transport. The shared involvement of Slc5a1 in these processes implies a possible mechanistic link between Dapagliflozin and Slc5a1, particularly through the regulation of glucose homeostasis. However, the direct interaction between Dapagliflozin and Slc5a1 remains unconfirmed, and further experimental validation is needed to establish a precise mechanism of action.",
